Now cue the water works.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:57.850
Number 1 - The Truth Field Goes Beyond Trenzalore.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:01.860
This is a bit meta, but Steven Moffat wrote
in jokes addressing everyone’s comments

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:07.600
about the 13th regeneration and the rule of
12 and all the other logic problems.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.830
I loved how the doctor literally spoke everyone’s
biggest questions out loud as if to say, yes

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.620
we know we know there’s some issues.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:18.790
A lot of fans have complained in the past
that steven moffat doesn’t care about canon

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:23.960
established during classic who, without spoiling
anything I can safely say that the episode

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:27.640
assures us that he does and it all makes sense.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.880
Number 2 - Tying everything up with a nice
bowtie.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.140
Most if not all of the major ongoing plot
threads from matt smith’s run are tied up

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:37.450
going all the way back to the eleventh hour.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:41.409
I was so happy to finally get a definitive
answer about the logic behind some of the

00:01:41.409 --> 00:01:45.900
more universe altering events that happened
during the big bang, namely the tardis exploding

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.450
and the cracks in the universe.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:51.940
I’ll go into greater detail about all those
plot threads and their solutions in that breakdown

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.050
video.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.310
Number 3 - The turkey is done.

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:58.970
The tone of the episode was this perfect blend
of sadness and humor.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:03.560
I spent most of the episode in a state somewhere
between both.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.250
But there was this strong undercurrent of
hope.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.250
I can say this without spoiling anything.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.979
That moment where the doctor says I have a
plan, then immediately turns to clara and

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:13.370
says no i haven’t got a plan, but people
love it when i say that.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:17.970
is a great explanation of how even though
everything you see on screen tells you something

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:22.740
awful is supposed to happen, the doctor can
make you feel okay about it.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.830
Number 4 - deus ex machina.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:29.950
A big criticism of some of steven moffat’s
stories is the deus ex machina solutions to

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.340
the doctor’s problems.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:36.560
The solution to the seige of trenzalore and
the 13th regeneration felt totally justified

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:37.560
this time.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:42.349
What i mean is that the solution flows completely
from events in the 50th anniversary episode

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:46.220
as well as some of the finer plot points set
up during matt smith’s run.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:51.190
To be fair it incorporates logic from series
5, series 6 and series 7.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:55.319
But including all those bits just makes the
transition from matt smith to peter capaldi

00:02:55.319 --> 00:02:56.670
that much more epic.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.510
Number 5 - The regeneration.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:03.570
Having made so many doctor who videos this
year I thought I was prepared to see the regeneration.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:06.459
But there was this one moment that just pushed
me over the edge.

00:03:06.459 --> 00:03:10.410
I don’t want to spoil it, but there’s
a very surprise cameo that made the whole

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.220
experience perfect for me.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:14.930
And I’m still crying inside a little bit.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:18.540
Not about Matt Smith, but about that moment
during the cameo.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.020
Number 6 - Welcome Peter Capaldi.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:25.090
Peter capaldi was on screen for only a few
minutes, but I loved it.

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:28.750
And he utters this question to clara that
gives you an idea of what the first couple

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.410
of episodes of series 8 are going to be like.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.280
I also loved the outfit.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:36.800
I’ll talk more specifically about that during
my breakdown tomorrow.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.930
But the question of capaldi’s outfit is
largely answered.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:45.550
Matt Smith changed his outfit several times
from series to series, so capaldi will change

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:46.550
his eventually too.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:51.099
But I expect that thematically, a few of the
affectations we saw in this outfit will stick.

00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:52.830
Namely the issue of neckwear.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.349
Careful for spoilers in my next one.

00:03:54.349 --> 00:03:58.300
I’m going to be ranking the episode against
other regenerations and need to include some

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.300
plot points.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.849
so turn the volume down if you need to.

00:04:01.849 --> 00:04:03.850
Number 7 - Ranking The Episode.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:07.530
How does it stack up against other recent
regeneration episodes?

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:11.780
Because this episode was a little more bombastic
than David Tennant’s and christopher eccleston’s

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:17.000
ending and we knew ahead of time that clara
would be staying on as the companion, it didn’t

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.959
have the air of finality or palor of sadness
to it that the end of time or parting of ways

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:21.959
had.

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:26.620
But from an overall satisfaction standpoint
I would rank this as number one.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:30.620
Just because it became the beginning of a
whole new regeneration cycle.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:33.330
Meaning the doctor doesn’t have as much
to lose anymore.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.870
He has life to burn.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:39.090
Which for me is so exciting because it means
he can start taking bigger chances.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:42.780
Hopefully the stories told during series 8
will reflect that.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:45.130
Okay you can turn the volume back up, spoilers
over.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.850
So if it wasn’t clear I loved the episode.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:51.160
It wasn’t as emotional a regeneration as
david tennant or christopher eccleston, but

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.380
it was definitely the most exciting.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:58.000
One of the hardest things to do on doctor
is one up yourself with each new doctor.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:08.140
And I feel like this episode raised the stakes
and the consequences without being ridiculous.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:12.550
I’ll be rewatching it at least four more
times...today.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:19.410
Without spoiling anything my favorite moment
was definitely the cameo at the end.

